# 45. Listing Users

You can inspect local user entries using:

```bash
cat /etc/passwd
```

However, `/etc/passwd` may contain both human users and system/service accounts.

A more accurate way to understand local account ranges is to inspect the UID values configured by the distribution rather than assuming every entry is a human user.

